.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMO-LIST-ALERTS 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emo-list-alerts \- show where every series an alert rule judges stands now
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli emo list-alerts
[\fB\-\-rule\-id\fR|\fB\-r\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-state\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fISTATE\fR]
[\fB\-\-active\fR|\fB\-a\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
One entry per rule and series: its state, since when, the last figure
judged and when that row was written, and \- beside them \- the rule's
metric, statistic, comparison, lines and description, so an entry can be
read without looking the rule up.
.PP
A series appears once its rule has judged a row of it, which is at the
first period's flush after the rule was created, or after the series
first reported. It disappears when its rule is deleted, disabled or
pointed at other series.
.PP
.I lastSeen
is the start of the period the last row covers. A series whose
.I lastSeen
is falling behind has stopped reporting; a rule with
.I noDataAfterPeriods
says so by itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule\-id " " \fIID\fR
Only this rule's series.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-state " " \fISTATE\fR
Only series in this state:
.BR OK ,
.BR WARNING ,
.B CRITICAL
or
.BR NO_DATA .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-active
Only series that are not OK \- what is wrong right now.
.SH OUTPUT
.RS
.nf
{"items": [{"ruleId": "system-cpu-per-host", "name": "system-cpu-usage",
            "labels": {"host": "vogje01-pios"}, "state": "WARNING",
            "severity": "warning", "since": "2026-10-31T12:05:00Z",
            "value": 83.4, "lastSeen": "2026-10-31T12:10:00Z",
            "statistic": "value", "comparison": "above",
            "warning": 80, "critical": 90, "description": "...",
            "namespace": "development"}]}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The alerts were printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated, or is not an administrator.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# What is wrong right now
euclid-cli emo list-alerts --active

# Only the critical ones
euclid-cli emo list-alerts --state CRITICAL

# Every host one rule judges
euclid-cli emo list-alerts --rule-id system-cpu-per-host
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emo (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-list-alert-history (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-list-alert-rules (1)
